  "id": "COMPOUND:29579 - PROTEIN:4928",
  "verbalization": "Ingenol-20-decanoate is implicated in the targeting of T-cell surface glycoprotein CD3 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Ingenol-20-decanoate acts as a target for multiple compounds, all of which ultimately lead to the activation or modulation of CD3. This indicates a potential pathway where Ingenol-20-decanoate may influence cellular processes through its interaction with Malme-3M, a cell line that is targeted by various compounds, including those that ultimately affect CD3. The shared targeting of CD3 across different compounds implies a possible functional link between these molecules, possibly through common downstream effects on T-cell signaling or function. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Ingenol-20-decanoate in modulating T-cell activity, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
